From d07c67ecfc01f5cc97e9589edd9467c84128a954 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:18:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fail the static build if browser storage is ever
 introduced

The customer-facing site uses no localStorage, sessionStorage or IndexedDB,
and should stay that way. build-static.sh now greps the built output and
exits non-zero if any of them appear, so a Render deploy fails loudly rather
than shipping them.

Verified: the build exits 1 when localStorage is present and 0 when it is not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHRkqpijyrVnGpHMk66YGP
---
 build-static.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 build-static.sh

diff --git a/build-static.sh b/build-static.sh
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index a6e9a14..ef96008
--- a/build-static.sh
+++ b/build-static.sh
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@ fi
 cp -r public/images dist/images
 [ -d public/products_images ] && cp -r public/products_images dist/products_images
 
+# Guard: the customer-facing site must never use browser storage. If any of
+# these appear, the build fails rather than shipping them.
+if grep -rn "localStorage\|sessionStorage\|indexedDB\|openDatabase" dist/ ; then
+  echo "ERROR: browser storage found in the built site (listed above). Remove it." >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+echo "Checked: no browser storage used."
+
 # Anything not matched by a file falls back to the homepage.
 cp dist/index.html dist/404.html
 
-- 
2.43.0

